# Commit attribution — Kassa only

Every commit in this repository is **Kassa's own work**. This is enforced in CI by
`scripts/check_commit_attribution.py` and must never be violated by an agent.

> This file is the Cursor-specific copy. The committed, tool-neutral version of these rules —
> plus everything else a first change has to satisfy — is in `CONTRIBUTING.md` at the repo
> root. Keep the two in agreement; `CONTRIBUTING.md` is the one every tool and every human
> can read, and for a while it did not exist, so this file was the *only* place the rule
> below was written down.

## Hard rules

When creating commits (or PR bodies that accompany them):

- **Author / committer:** use only the identity already configured in this repo
  (e.g. `KassaSana` with an allowed email). Do **not** change `git config`, and do
  **not** pass `--author` to invent or substitute another person.
- **Never** add `Co-Authored-By:` trailers of any kind.
- **Never** add "Generated with …", "Made with Cursor", "Co-contributor", or any
  AI / Cursor / vendor attribution footer.
- **Never** list Cursor, Claude, Copilot, or any tool as a contributor, co-author,
  or committer — in commit messages, PR bodies, or docs that claim authorship of code.
- Prose that *names* a tool (e.g. explaining a filename) is fine; claiming that tool
  wrote the code is not.

If a hook or tool tries to append attribution automatically, strip it before the
commit succeeds. A bad attribution commit is permanent history; do not land it.
